<%= render layout: "guides/frame", locals: { guide: @guide } do %>
  <p>
    Whether the small-dispenser exemption covers your pharmacy comes down to one number on one date. It takes
    ten minutes to work out and write down, and it is the first thing to settle before deciding anything else
    about DSCSA.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The test</h2>
    <%= render "guides/qualify" %>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who counts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Licensed pharmacists and qualified pharmacy technicians</strong> who are full-time employees.
        Clerks, drivers and other staff are not part of the count.</li>
      <li><strong>Full-time means the IRS test:</strong> 30 or more hours a week, or 130 a month. The test counts
        full-time employees, so staff who work fewer hours are not counted.</li>
      <li><strong>One date:</strong> the count is taken as of <%= DscsaDeadline.qualifying_label %>, not averaged
        over the year.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If you own more than one store</h2>
    <p>
      The count is for the <strong>company that owns the pharmacy</strong>, not each store on its own. An owner
      with three stores of eight full-time pharmacists and technicians each has 24, and qualifies; add a fourth
      store and the company is over 25, so none of the stores qualify. If your stores are owned through more than
      one company, or you have joined a larger group, check which company owns each pharmacy before you count.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Write it down</h2>
    <p>
      FDA doesn&rsquo;t ask you to file anything, which is exactly why it&rsquo;s worth a record. A one-page
      worksheet kept with your DSCSA file is enough:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The owning company&rsquo;s legal name and each pharmacy it owns.</li>
      <li>For each licensed pharmacist and qualified technician: name, role, and usual weekly hours as of
        <%= DscsaDeadline.qualifying_label %>.</li>
      <li>The full-time total, the date you counted, and who counted.</li>
      <li>A note of which trading partners you told that you rely on the exemption, and when.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If you&rsquo;re over 25</h2>
    <p>
      The exemption doesn&rsquo;t apply, and the enhanced, package-level requirements already apply to your
      pharmacy. Talk to your wholesalers and your pharmacy-system vendor now about how they exchange and verify
      that data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Either way</h2>
    <p>These obligations apply whether or not you qualify:</p>
    <%= render "guides/applies_today" %>
  </section>
<% end %>
